- Read AGENTS.md
- Extrapolate and apply design patterns
- Apply DRY principals
- You are using object oriented design. Keep data and logic together in pydantic classes.
- Push functionality and logic down into cohesive classes
- Do not use dicts if objects exists
- Use object fields rather than dict keys
- Wrapper methods or functions are FORBIDDEN! Refactor and simplify instead.
- Do not worry about backwards compatibility unless there is already stored data in the database
- After updating test files, always run the affected tests to verify the changes